{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p10-902041b0","text":"Screenshot always 844x1340 regardless of viewport height, so it's capturing the browser's visible panel fixed at 1340 device px (1072 CSS). The fullPage screenshot was 844x1500 (675x1200 CSS) and included footer? It had duplicate content because page height 1200? Wait fullPage image 844x1500 = 675x1200 CSS, exactly stage height. But it showed a second header at bottom, which suggests the stage wasn't scrolled? Maybe the fullPage image is actually two stacked copies because the page content height was 2400? No, 1500/1.25=1200. The second header in the image at y~1540 (of 1500?) impossible—the displayed image was 844x1500 but I saw content beyond? The rendering may show 1500 height but looked like 1730? Hmm. Actually the fullPage image from the transcript was 844x1500 (aspect 0.562) and showed the stage from top to stats at ~1350 and a second header at 1540—out of 1500? The visual could be distorted. Not reliable.

The screenshot tool appears limited to the browser panel's visible area (844x1340), and fullPage might capture document length. With viewport CSS height 1328 but panel only 1072, screenshot captures only 1072. So to see footer, use fullPage=true. The page document height is 1328; fullPage should produce 844x1660 (1328*1.25). But it produced 844x1500 for the previous viewport 1200: 1200*1.25=1500. Good. It captured full document 1200 but the stage top maybe 64? Wait previous viewport 675x1200 had docH=1200, stage from 0 to 1200, fullPage 1500. The screenshot showed duplicate content after stats—maybe because the stage is vertically centered with height 1200 and the page was scrolled? No scroll.

Could be fullPage screenshot stitching bug with `position: fixed` duplicates. The second header at bottom could be the browser's overlay? Hard.

We can crop the fullPage screenshot to the stage top 0..1200 if we can identify. But duplicate remains near bottom. For README, we can use an earlier good screenshot (`obs-stage-final.png` old) and not worry about credit line visual. The layout is verified via DOM: footer/credit within stage at y1184-1194. That's sufficient. We don't need to embed a new screenshot. The current README screenshot is old but clean and faithful except no credit line; could update to a new image using the fullPage but crop to avoid duplicates, if possible.

Let's inspect `obs-stage-full-check.png` dimensions 844x1500 and view it with separate crop. The duplicate second header appeared at bottom; maybe that's actually the stage's footer region? No, clearly a second "LIVE PRAYER ROOM / CHRISTIAN PRAYER LIVE" line. Could be because fullPage screenshot was taken while the stage had scrolled internally? Wait the page may contain two `.stage-9x16` elements? Let's count. `document.querySelectorAll('.stage-9x16').length` likely 1. Duplicate is weird.

Maybe the image is 844x1500 but chat displayed it with an overlapping duplicate from another layer due the browser overlay (the screenshot tool's "Freebuff" badge repeated at bottom indicating a second screenshot stitched at scroll position). FullPage screenshot stitching often produces overlapping duplicates if page height is fractional and fixed elements; yes, the tool may stitch two viewport captures and include overlap. So avoid fullPage.

Solution: change preview viewport so the *panel visible height* covers 1200 CSS stage. The panel height is fixed by the app, ~1072 CSS; cannot. But we can zoom out the page (`preview_evaluate document.body.style.zoom = ...`) or scale stage to fit 1072 while keeping 9:16: set `--stage-scale` manually to 1072/1920 = 0.558, so stage becomes 603x1072 and fits entirely in the visible screenshot, with side margins. Then screenshot captures full stage. This is just for the screenshot artifact. We can set stage scale via JS `document.querySelector('.stage-9x16').style.transform = 'translate(-50%,-50%) scale(0.558)'`, but stage wrapper is 675x1328, centered; the stage will fit vertically with 603 width. Screenshot 844x1340 includes margins. Crop stage: width 603*1.25=754, height 1072*1.25=1340, top 0. Image 844x1340. Crop x=(844-754)/2=45, y=0. The stage includes footer. This yields a full 9:16 stage screenshot at 754x1340, no badge (badge overlays top-left 0-50; stage starts at x=45, badge overlaps stage at x45-? The badge is at x14-94 CSS? If stage starts x36 CSS, badge overlaps the stage header. But we can hide the badge element (`div` with Freebuff text) before screenshot? It's an injected overlay; we could `document.querySelectorAll('div').find(...)` and hide. Better find element whose textContent==='Freebuff' and remove/hide. This is not app content; okay for artifact.

Also set stage wrapper background dark, margins. Or use CSS to zoom stage. Simpler: after reload v=11, set:
```
const st=document.querySelector('.stage-9x16');
st.style.transform='translate(-50%,-50%) scale(0.5583)';
[...document.querySelectorAll('*')].filter(el=>el.childElementCount===0 && el.textContent.trim()==='Freebuff').forEach(el=>el.parentElement.style.display='none');
```
The Freebuff badge may be in a shadow DOM or injected via an overlay div; find. Could instead crop top 50? Stage top centered: wrapper 1328, stage 1072, top=(1328-1072)/2=128 CSS (160 image). Badge at y~15-41 CSS (19-51 image) is above stage (starts 128), so cropping stage at y=160 removes badge. Perfect! No need hide.

Set stage scale 0.5583 manually. Then evaluate rect: stage top 128, bottom 1200. Screenshot visible 1072 CSS (1340 image) captures 0-1072, so stage bottom 1200 is beyond visible! Wait panel visible CSS height is 1072, despite viewport 1328. Stage wrapper likely 1328, stage centered at 128-1200; visible screenshot captures 0-1072, cutting bottom 128. Need stage scale/fit to visible area 1072, plus account for wrapper center at 1328: set scale such that stage height ≤1072 and top ≥? Center of wrapper 664; stage 1072 → top 128. Visible 0-1072 cuts bottom. Need shift the stage up so it fits 0-1072: set `top: 50%` but wrapper center 664; stage top 128. If we set stage `top: 536px` (half of 1072) then top 0, bottom 1072. Or set wrapper height to 1072? Easier:
```
st.style.top='536px'; st.style.transform='translate(-50%,-50%) scale(0.5583)';
```
With stage height 1920*0.5583=1072, top=536, so top 0, bottom 1072. Perfect for visible capture. Width = 603, centered, side margins 36. Then screenshot visible 675x1072 CSS, image 844x1340; crop x=45, width 754, y=0 height 1340. 9:16? 754/1340=0.5627, yes.

This is purely for the README screenshot; app CSS unchanged. But it also visually verifies footer/credit. Do it after reload. The page may have resize observer resetting transform on viewport resize, but we won't resize. `fitStage` isn't called by style changes. Good.

Set top 536px and scale 0.5583. Also stage-wrapper overflow hidden at 1328? The stage gets moved up within wrapper, but the wrapper starts at y=0 and has height 1328; visible screenshot y 0-1072. Fine.

Then screenshot to temp, crop, save final. Need ensure state is clean (yes). The image will show stage full, including footer/credit. Great.

