{"kind":"reasoning","id":"p12-902041b0","text":"Now we see full stage and footer/credit. But there's a weird overlay at right bottom around y=930-1060 (a ghost panel with "2" and small text). This is the quick dock? In OBS mode quick dock hidden. It looks like a transparent duplicate of comments/community, perhaps because we scaled stage manually and there's an element outside? Actually at right edge, x=725-819, there's a faint duplicate of counters and text. Could be the browser's right-side scrollbar? Or another stage layer? Wait the stage width after crop from 45 to 799; original screenshot width 844. The ghost at 725-819 lies within stage 45-799 partly and outside. It may be the stage content from another element? In screenshot at 725-819, there's a semi-transparent "2" and rows. Could be the quick dock *behind* the stage, visible beyond stage right edge because we shifted stage up but not clipped horizontally? Quick dock should be hidden in obs mode. The layout body has stage-wrapper + quick-dock; body.obs-mode hides it. But we added `?obs=1`; body should have obs-mode. It seems visible behind.

