# CHRISTIAN PRAYER LIVE — Conversion Complete

The existing Bun/TikTok Live RPC application has been converted in place into a general Christian prayer livestream for the US market. The original JSON-RPC architecture, TikTok event pipeline, WebSocket layer, 9:16 OBS stage, admin dashboard, Python environment and Piper models were preserved.

The server is currently running at:

- Stage: **http://localhost:3000**
- OBS clean source: **http://localhost:3000/?obs=1**
- Admin: **http://localhost:3000/admin**

![Christian Prayer Live stage](docs/screenshots/obs-stage-final.png)

## What was implemented

| Area | Result |
| --- | --- |
| Brand | CHRISTIAN PRAYER LIVE, “FAITH • HOPE • LOVE”, “Pray Together. Grow in Faith.” |
| Visuals | Navy/gold/ivory church stage, glowing cross, licensed photography, soft overlays, particles |
| Stage | 1080×1920 layout, prayer request card, verse card, live comments, community activity, counters, footer |
| TikTok | Comments, likes, follows, shares and gifts mapped to Christian interactions |
| Prayer queue | Moderation with approve, hide, remove, pause, clear and auto-approve |
| Backgrounds | 19 local photographs, 6 categories, timed fade rotation, manual selection, thumbnails |
| TTS | Language-aware Piper worker, EN-US and VI-VN voices, queue, cache, admin tests |
| Admin | Full English dashboard for connection, prayer, audio, backgrounds, messages and RPC |
| Compatibility | Original `temple.*` methods, event names, OBS URL and state aliases retained |

User-facing Buddhist content was removed. Internal legacy names such as `temple.burnIncense` remain only as RPC compatibility identifiers.

## Images and licensing

Downloaded **19 photographs + 3 generated overlays** into [public/assets/christian](public/assets/christian), with full source, license and author records in [asset-manifest.json](public/assets/christian/asset-manifest.json).

| Category | Count |
| --- | --- |
| Church interiors | 4 |
| Altar crosses | 4 |
| Prayer candles | 4 |
| Sunrise/golden skies | 3 |
| Bible/communion | 2 |
| Christian artwork | 2 |
| Generated overlays | 3 |

Licenses: 9× CC BY-SA 3.0, 5× CC BY-SA 4.0, 1× CC BY 2.0, 1× CC BY 3.0, 1× CC0, 2× public domain, plus 3 generated CC0 overlays.

The stage now shows a subtle photo credit line for the active background, and the admin shows the full credit. **Keep the manifest with the project and include the required photographer credits in your video description.** All images are served locally; no remote image is requested during the stream.

## Piper voices detected

**English (3):**
- `en_US-amy-medium` — default
- `en_US-arctic-medium`
- `en_US-hfc_female-medium`

**Vietnamese (14):**
- `vi_VN-vais1000-medium` — default
- `banmai`, `chieuthanh`, `cuc`, `duyoryx3175`, `lacphi`, `maiphuong`, `manhdung`, `minhkhang`, `minhquang`, `ngochuyen`, `ngochuyennew`, `phuongtrang`, `taian2`

The rewritten [tts_worker.py](tts_worker.py) selects voices by language, loads models on demand, caches WAV output and keeps the existing browser narration queue serialized. English events use US English voices; Vietnamese text uses the Vietnamese voice. The admin has **Test English**, **Test Vietnamese**, volume, speed, language and enable/disable controls.

ZeroTTS was not retained as a fallback: the Windows checkout has no `zerotts` package and the old worker pointed to a macOS model directory, so it was not functional here. The original worker is preserved in [backup/tts_worker.py.bak](backup/tts_worker.py.bak).

## Verification actually performed

**Server/API:** 51/51 smoke checks passed via [scripts/smoke-test.js](scripts/smoke-test.js), including:

- Bun startup, `/api/health`, `/admin`, all static assets.
- `temple.getState` compatibility and new counters.
- 19-image background catalog, categories, local serving and manual changes.
- Prayer add/display/first-name privacy/pause/hide/remove.
- AMEN and PRAY commands, prayer-request detection and sanitization.
- English and Vietnamese Piper synthesis, WAV serving, cache hits, voice discovery.
- Settings updates, editable message library, tiered gift messages, Bible references.
- WebSocket JSON-RPC plus `prayer.request`, `temple.event` and `temple.state` notifications.

**TikTok connector:** initialized successfully and failed gracefully for a non-live handle with `Failed to retrieve Room ID from all sources.`; disconnect clears the stale channel/error state. No crash.

**Browser:** OBS mode rendered at the correct 1080×1920 aspect, AMEN overlay and event pipeline were exercised, prayer card and comments/community columns rendered, photo credit populated, footer placement verified, and the browser console had no JavaScript errors after the final reload. Admin connection, prayer moderation, voice controls and background grid were checked visually.

### Not tested here

- **A real TikTok LIVE session.** No live account was available, so actual comment/like/follow/share/gift events from TikTok were not observed end to end.
- **OBS Studio itself.** The page was verified in Chromium at the OBS aspect ratio, not captured inside OBS. Audio autoplay may require clicking **Enable Audio & Narration** once via OBS **Interact**.
- **Long-duration CPU/audio stability** over a multi-hour broadcast.
- **Native-speaker pronunciation review** of the generated English/Vietnamese audio.

## Main files

- [server.js](server.js) — HTTP, WebSocket, TikTok, RPC, prayer queue, rotation
- [tts_worker.py](tts_worker.py) — multilingual Piper worker
- [config/app.config.json](config/app.config.json) — settings
- [config/messages.en.json](config/messages.en.json) — editable messages and verified KJV verses
- [public/index.html](public/index.html) — livestream stage
- [public/admin.html](public/admin.html) — ministry dashboard
- [public/css/live.css](public/css/live.css), [public/js/live.js](public/js/live.js), [public/js/audio.js](public/js/audio.js)
- [public/assets/christian/asset-manifest.json](public/assets/christian/asset-manifest.json)
- [scripts/fetch_christian_assets.py](scripts/fetch_christian_assets.py) — reproducible licensed-image fetcher
- [scripts/smoke-test.js](scripts/smoke-test.js)
- [.env.example](.env.example)
- [README.md](README.md) — full setup, API, licensing and testing documentation
- [backup/](backup) — pre-conversion copies of modified files

## Windows startup

The environment is already installed. To start again:

```bat
cd /d "C:\xampp\htdocs\ai bpage anhang	iktok y tuong marketing\1"
bun run start
```

For a fresh machine:

```bat
bun install
uv venv .venv
uv pip install --python .venv\Scripts\python.exe piper-tts pillow
bun run start
```

Then open OBS with a Browser source at `http://localhost:3000/?obs=1`, **1080×1920**, and connect the TikTok account from `/admin` while it is live.

## Remaining notes

- The current room intentionally contains a two-request demo state. Clear it from the admin queue before going live.
- CC BY/BY-SA backgrounds require attribution; the on-stream credit and manifest are included for that purpose.
- This folder is not a Git repository, so no commit or push was made.
- The app is running with rotation enabled, TTS ready, default English voice `en_US-amy-medium`, and TikTok disconnected.

The next highest-value step is a real LIVE run to validate the actual TikTok payloads and OBS audio behavior.
