# Ambient Worship Music — Implemented and Verified

The app now has a continuous instrumental worship bed under the livestream. The old synthesized drone was replaced with five original 3+ minute tracks, a crossfading playlist, and automatic ducking whenever Piper narrates. The server is running at **http://localhost:3000/?obs=1** with *Peaceful Prayer* playing at 10%.

## Changed and created files

| File | Change |
| --- | --- |
| [scripts/generate_music.py](scripts/generate_music.py) | **New.** Composer/renderer that synthesizes five loop-safe instrumentals (pads, felt piano, strings, circular cathedral reverb) and writes the manifest |
| [public/assets/christian/audio/](public/assets/christian/audio) | **New.** Five Ogg Opus tracks (~14.8 MB total) plus [music-manifest.json](public/assets/christian/audio/music-manifest.json) |
| [public/js/audio.js](public/js/audio.js) | Replaced the oscillator ambience with a Web Audio playlist player: lazy decode, sample-accurate loops, two-deck crossfade, shuffle/repeat, fades, ducking, limiter |
| [public/js/live.js](public/js/live.js) | Loads `/api/music`, syncs settings/state, auto-advance persists to the server, dock controls, status text |
| [public/index.html](public/index.html) | Dock now shows the current track, previous/next, play-pause, shuffle and music status (still hidden in `?obs=1`) |
| [public/css/live.css](public/css/live.css) | Styling for the new dock music row |
| [public/admin.html](public/admin.html) | New **Background Music** panel |
| [public/js/admin.js](public/js/admin.js) | Music panel rendering, playlist, live controls, test player |
| [public/css/admin.css](public/css/admin.css) | Playlist row styling |
| [server.js](server.js) | Music catalog loader, persisted `settings.music`, `/api/music`, `music.*` RPC, `music.state` broadcast, health info |
| [config/config.js](config/config.js) | Music defaults and `MUSIC_*` environment overrides |
| [config/app.config.json](config/app.config.json) | 10% volume, 3.5% duck volume, default track, autoplay/shuffle/repeat |
| [.env.example](.env.example) | Documents the new `MUSIC_*` variables |
| [scripts/smoke-test.js](scripts/smoke-test.js) | Added six music checks |
| [README.md](README.md) | Music section, licenses, admin controls, config, API, test results |

## Music sources and licenses

All five tracks are **original compositions synthesized locally from scratch** by `scripts/generate_music.py` — no samples, no third-party recordings, no imitation of existing songs. They are dedicated to the **public domain (CC0 1.0)**; no attribution is required.

| Track | Mood | Tempo | Length |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `peaceful-prayer-01` | Warm pads, soft felt piano | 60 BPM | 3:28 |
| `peaceful-prayer-02` | String ensemble over slow harmony | 56 BPM | 3:09 |
| `cathedral-ambient-01` | Deep organ-like ambience, wide reverb | 52 BPM | 3:14 |
| `piano-worship-01` | Solo felt piano arpeggios | 66 BPM | 3:24 |
| `morning-prayer-01` | Bright piano with sunrise pads | 72 BPM | 3:20 |

No vocals, no drums, no percussion; peak −1 dBFS, no clipping. Each file is rendered on a circular timeline and convolved with a circular reverb, so the last sample joins the first without a gap.

## Controls

**Admin → Background Music:** enable/disable, play/pause, previous/next, track selector, volume, shuffle, repeat (playlist / one / once), autoplay toggle, **Test Audio**, live status and the full playlist. Changes are stored server-side and pushed over the WebSocket, so the OBS source follows without reloading or restarting.

**Quick dock** (desktop stage only): track name, previous/next, play/pause, shuffle, music volume.

## Audio mixing

Music defaults to **10%**; narration stays at **95%**. When Piper starts, the music bus glides to **3.5%**, then restores over roughly two seconds. A limiter sits on the music bus, and TTS never routes through it, so the two cannot clip each other. Only one music deck plays at a time (plus a short intentional crossfade).

## Tests actually run

- **57/57** smoke checks pass, including new checks for 5 tracks, 3–5 minute lengths, 10%/3.5% defaults, local file serving and track change without restart.
- Chromium stage at 1080×1920: autoplay starts, `AudioContext` running, five-track playlist, correct current track, no console errors.
