### Rescan — where it is
**`/admin` → Background Music panel → the gold “🔄 Rescan Music Folder” button** at the top of the panel, next to the search box and category filter.

It scans only `public/assets/christian/audio/`, recognizes `.mp3 .wav .ogg .m4a .flac`, and:
- adds new files with friendly titles (`soft-piano-prayer.mp3` → “Soft Piano Prayer”) and marks their license **Unknown — verify before publishing** rather than guessing;
- drops files missing from disk;
- refreshes size, duration and format with `ffprobe`;
- preserves custom titles, enabled flags and license metadata;
- writes the manifest atomically and keeps `music-manifest.backup.json`;
- broadcasts `music.library.updated` so the dashboard and stage refresh without a restart.

The result line reads, for example: `Music library synchronized! 22 tracks found · 1 new · 0 missing · 0 metadata updates.` New files also raise a “set its title, category and license” notice.

### Dashboard
Each row now shows an editable title, status (Playing / Previewing / Disabled / Ready), duration, format, size, category, preview play/pause, per-track preview volume, Enable/Disable and Remove. Remove asks for confirmation and moves the audio to `docs/backups/music-removed/`. The panel also has search, category filter, total track count and total playlist duration. Existing shuffle, repeat, next/previous, master volume and test-audio controls remain.

### Playback safety
