## Copyright Safe Broadcast Mode — implemented

**Copyright Safe Mode is ON by default.** Automatic background rotation, scene matching, manual background selection, music playback, and track changes now accept only assets that are:

- present in `config/copyright-manifest.json`
- marked **VERIFIED**
- active broadcast assets
- permitted for commercial, livestream, TikTok, and OBS use
- still present on disk

Missing manifest entries are blocked. Filenames and folder locations never upgrade an asset’s status. No asset was deleted or had its status changed.

### Exact eligibility count

| Metric | Count |
| --- | ---: |
| Active broadcast assets | **45** |
| **Eligible for broadcast** | **30** |
| Blocked | **15** |
| Automatic rotation assets | **27** — 6 backgrounds + 21 music tracks |
| Fixed verified stage overlays | **3** |

The 15 blocked assets are the CC BY-SA cathedral, church, Bible, cross, and candle images. Their files, manifests, and credits remain intact; they are simply excluded while safe mode is on. The full inventory is in [COPYRIGHT_AUDIT.md](docs/COPYRIGHT_AUDIT.md).

### Runtime protection

- Server-side checks are in [lib/broadcast-safety.js](lib/broadcast-safety.js) and [server.js](server.js).
- The OBS page independently re-checks `/copyright-audit.json` in [live.js](public/js/live.js), so a stale server event cannot display a blocked image.
- Blocked background attempts are logged with the exact reason and fall back to a verified image. If none exists, the stage clears safely.
- Blocked music is skipped, logged, and the selection is repaired to the first eligible track. If no eligible track exists, music pauses safely.
- With safe mode off, only an explicit administrator choice can select a blocked asset. This was tested separately.

### Admin controls

At `http://localhost:3000/admin`, inside **Copyright & Licensing**:

- **Copyright Safe Mode ON/OFF** toggle
- **30 eligible / 15 blocked / 30 selectable now**
- **Blocked only** filter
- blocked-asset reasons and manual-review status
- **Attribution preview**
- existing rescan button and full audit inventory

![Copyright Safe Mode admin panel](docs/screenshots/admin-copyright-safe-mode.png)

### Attribution

Only **2 currently eligible images** require attribution:

- **Prayer Candles (5406060261).jpg** — Serge Melki, CC BY 2.0
- **Nave of Basilica Saint-Sernin - 2012-08-24.jpg** — PierreSelim, CC BY 3.0

The other 28 eligible assets are public domain, CC0, generated, or Mixkit tracks requiring no credit. The consolidated list is at [ASSET_ATTRIBUTION.md](docs/ASSET_ATTRIBUTION.md), and the admin panel has a copy-ready preview.

### Files changed

- [server.js](server.js) — eligibility enforcement, safe-mode toggle, startup repair, rotation/music guards, audit RPCs
- [lib/broadcast-safety.js](lib/broadcast-safety.js) — shared VERIFIED/permission/file eligibility layer
- [lib/copyright-audit.js](lib/copyright-audit.js) — regenerated attribution document with eligible-asset section
- [public/js/live.js](public/js/live.js) — OBS client-side guard and fallback
- [public/js/admin.js](public/js/admin.js) — safe-mode controls, counts, blocked view, attribution preview
- [public/admin.html](public/admin.html) and [public/css/admin.css](public/css/admin.css) — admin panel UI
- [scripts/smoke-test.js](scripts/smoke-test.js) — safe-mode coverage
- [README.md](README.md) — safe-mode documentation and API methods
- [docs/ASSET_ATTRIBUTION.md](docs/ASSET_ATTRIBUTION.md), [docs/COPYRIGHT_AUDIT.md](docs/COPYRIGHT_AUDIT.md), [public/copyright-audit.json](public/copyright-audit.json), and the screenshot above

### Verification actually run

- **Full smoke suite: 142/142 checks passed** on an isolated server instance, including safe-mode counts, blocked-background rejection, rotation eligibility, safe-mode bypass/restore, music, TTS, quiz, prayer queue, congregation, OBS assets, and WebSocket notifications.
- **Eligibility unit checks: 8/8 passed** — VERIFIED image accepted; NEEDS_REVIEW, UNKNOWN, missing manifest entry, missing file, and unverified music rejected; explicit safe-mode-off bypass accepted.
- **Targeted music checks passed** — unverified music blocked, safe-mode-off selection accepted, and safe mode restored to an eligible track.
- **OBS client check** — the currently running stage pointed at a blocked Bible image, logged `[Copyright] Background blocked … NEEDS_REVIEW`, and fell back to verified `backgrounds-01-golden-clouds.jpg` without JavaScript errors.
- **Startup check** — clean log: `[Copyright] Safe Mode ON — 6/21 backgrounds and 21/21 music files are eligible for broadcast.`

### One live-process limitation

I did not interrupt the livestream process already listening on port 3000. The updated OBS client guard is already active because it is served from the changed public files, but the **server-side safe-mode toggle and new RPCs require a normal restart** to become active in that process.

On Windows, from the project directory:

```bash
bun start
```

Then reload:

- OBS: `http://localhost:3000/?obs=1`
- Admin: `http://localhost:3000/admin`

