Fixed and verified. Here is the complete report.

## Root cause

The rotation pool was gated by a single stored value, `state.settings.background.category`, in three places:

1. `backgroundPool()` filtered the catalog to that one category (falling back to "all" only if empty).
2. `applyProgramContent()` overwrote that value with the program's preferred category on every schedule transition (`backgroundCategories` in `config/schedule.json`).
3. `applySceneForCue()` overwrote it again on every show cue (welcome → cathedral, verse → bible, healing → candles, …).

On top of that, `config/app.config.json` shipped `"category": "cathedral"`, and the persisted live state had `category: "bible"` with `randomize: false` — so the stage was walking just the 4 bible images in order. That is exactly the reported symptom.

## Exact logic changed ([server.js](server.js))

- `backgroundPool()` is now `eligibleStageImages()` — the whole catalog, filtered only by Copyright Safe Mode. This single pool feeds the timer, `stage.nextBackground`, and program starts. No second engine, no second timer.
- `programBackgroundCategory()` was deleted; `programBackgroundImage()` now draws from `backgroundPool()` and only replaces a missing/blocked current image.
- `applyProgramContent()` no longer writes `settings.background.category`; a program switch can no longer narrow anything.
- `applySceneForCue()` now returns early while auto-rotation is on (the pool owns the stage) and keeps its category-specific pick only when rotation is off, where the category is still recorded for the Admin grid.

Copyright gate, manual selection (`stage.setBackground`), notification names, RPC methods, manifests, intervals and fades are untouched.

## Files modified

| File | Change |
| --- | --- |
| [server.js](server.js) | Global pool, program no longer narrows, scene cue gated on rotation |
| [scripts/smoke-test.js](scripts/smoke-test.js) | Scene-match test now runs with rotation off; added two checks: a cue never replaces a rotating image, and the pool spans all 7 categories |
| [public/js/admin.js](public/js/admin.js) | One hint line: auto-rotation uses every eligible image in all categories |
| [public/admin.html](public/admin.html) | Note clarified: scene matching applies while rotation is off |
| [README.md](README.md) | Rotation-pool and scene-matching docs updated; `BACKGROUND_CATEGORY` described as a grid filter |

## Tests actually executed

Isolated instance on port **3120** (live state backed up first), then:

- `node --check` on `server.js`, `scripts/smoke-test.js`, `public/js/admin.js`, `public/js/live.js` — all OK.
- Rotation pool: **16 of 31** images eligible in Safe Mode, spanning **all 7 categories** (`backgrounds,bible,candles,cathedral,church,cross,jesus`).
- Sequential full cycle under each program — `morning`, `afternoon`, `evening`, `night`: **16/16** images visited and **7/7** categories under every one (8/8 checks).
- `stage.nextBackground`, manual pick, blocked pick, and persistence: **11/11** checks. Safe Mode rejection returned `Copyright status is NEEDS_REVIEW, not VERIFIED` and left the current image unchanged.
- Real timer at a 10 s interval: image changed and walked 4 different categories over six ticks.
- Existing suites: **smoke 168/168**, **reliability 77/77**.

Cleanup: test server stopped, `data/prayer-state.json` restored to its pre-test copy, test log removed, and the music manifest/backup that the test instance touched restored to HEAD. No commits made; pre-existing uncommitted work untouched.

## Limitations

- The 15 `NEEDS_REVIEW` images are still excluded — that is the Safe Mode contract, not a rotation restriction; making them eligible requires licence evidence, not a code change.
- Scene matching no longer overrides the stage while rotation is on; that is a deliberate contract change so the global pool owns the stage. With rotation off it behaves as before.
- Rotation avoids repeating the immediately previous image (pre-existing behaviour); repeats across the cycle are allowed as requested.
- No server was listening on port 3000, so nothing live was interrupted. The new code needs a normal `bun run server.js` start; no rebuild or config migration.

The rotation pool is now global, so the next worthwhile step is deciding which of the 15 blocked images you actually want licensed and cleared for air.
